
terms:

  pair: a net of the form (x first second)
  function: a net of the form (x input output)
  reference: a net of the form (x value space)
  sequence: a net of the form (x el0 (x el1 (x el2 ... (e) ... )))

  true: the net (x (x o (e)) o)
  false: the net (x (x (e) o) o)
  boolean: either true or false

  trigger: the net (x (y a b) (x a b)); construction: xyhhxsluul
  package: a duplicatable function whose input is a trigger
  fork: a duplicatable function that takes a trigger and outputs a pair of triggers

  library: a sequence of packages outputing various useful primitives
  number: a duplicatable black-box representing a 32-bit natural number manipulatable only by library functions

  stack: a primary stack of values, manipulated by most operations
  hold: a secondary stack of values, manipulated by a few operations
  memory: the stack and the hold

required operations:

  [x]-node: pop (x a b); push b; push a
  [y]-node: pop (y a b); push b; push a
  [e]raser: pop (e)
  [w]ire: push a; push a
  [l]ink: pop a; pop a

  [h]old: pop x; push x to hold
  [u]nhold: pop x from hold; push x
  [s]wap: pop x; pop y from hold; push x to hold; push y

  [b]ootstrap: halt execution; pop engine; link engine to (x io (x library ...))
  [p]rint: halt execution; link current memory to output, to render to user (development only)

required library:
  read: a function that takes a reference to io and outputs a number representing the read character
  eq: a function that takes a pair of numbers and outputs a boolean representing whether the numbers are equal

conventions:

  memory:
    { ... s2 s1 s0 | h0 h1 h2 ... }
    "s0 is the top of the stack, followed by s1 and s2, and h0 is the top of the hold, followed by h1 and h2"

  linking:
    a hold operation may be immediately followed by a name
    held port names come in pairs; two held ports with the same name should be linked
    ...

hold function to access the boot context

  WXLH

{ | boot_fn }

get the library:

  WHa
  WX
    X Hb X Y Ha Hc Hd
    X Hb X Hc Hd

  a b a c d b c d
  - - 0 - - 1 1 2
  2: U SUSU UL HH
  1: U SU   UL H
  1: U SU   UL H
  0: U      UL

  append
  XUXHLWSHXULL

{ library | boot_fn }

